  keySpec: Three reconfigurable displays
  summary: Orion's glass cockpit. Apollo carried over 500 switches and dials; Orion
    replaces almost all of it with three reconfigurable screens, borrowing heavily
    from the Boeing 787 flight deck.
  whyItMatters: 'Fewer physical switches means less mass and fewer failure points.
    The switches that remain are the ones that must work when the software does not:
    abort, and core life support.'
  narration: {fileID: 0}
